      "data": {
        "text": "**Choosing CloudWatch Logs**\n\nI've decided to proceed with AWS CloudWatch Logs as the external logging provider and will utilize the `boto3` library for integration. This approach provides a robust and widely adopted solution for logging within the AWS ecosystem, offering scalability and manageability.\n\n\n**Defining the Implementation**\n\nI'm now focusing on the Python script, `write_correlated_logs.py`. The aim is to integrate `boto3` to write logs to CloudWatch Logs with correlation IDs. My current plan is to create a function that handles writing log events and incorporates provider-specific information for robust logging. The script is the next task!\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789821327890,
          "start": 1789821324495
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0b9aa0ccf001P764De3EhztjXV",
      "message_id": "msg_0b9aa0764001g8OkqGmoz7qCSX",
